# rwcli reference

`rwcli` is the RayWaves package CLI. It is not inside the project folder.
Projects get a wrapper that points at the installed copy.

## Run it

From the project root (the folder with `project.raywaves`):

```text
@RWCLI_WRAPPER@ doctor . --json
@RWCLI_WRAPPER@ build . --json
@RWCLI_WRAPPER@ run . --frames 60 --json
```

If the wrapper is missing or stale:

```text
cat .raywaves/tooling.ini                  # Linux
# Get-Content .raywaves\tooling.ini       # Windows
# then call the path in [rwcli] path
```

If neither exists, open the project in RayWaves once, or run `rwcli lsp` from
the package. Do not guess the package location.

`tooling.ini` has `[rwcli] available=1|0`, `path`, `packageRoot`, `engineRoot`,
and `version`. `available=0` means the package CLI was not found when the
project was opened; build `rwcli` or install it on `PATH`. The wrapper falls
back to `where` on Windows and `command -v` on Linux.

Shell notes:

- Windows: `@RWCLI_WRAPPER@` is `.raywaves\bin\rwcli.cmd`; Linux:
  `.raywaves/bin/rwcli`.
- `rwcli` alone is not on `PATH`; use the generated wrapper or the absolute path.
- Engine logs go to stderr. Suppress them when capturing JSON:
  ```powershell
  $project = (Get-Location).Path
  $json = & @RWCLI_WRAPPER@ info $project --json 2>$null | ConvertFrom-Json
  ```
  ```sh
  json=$(@RWCLI_WRAPPER@ info . --json 2>/dev/null)
  ```
- Quote paths containing spaces.
- `--json` may appear anywhere after the command.

## Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `help [command]` | general or per-command usage |
| `--version` | CLI/engine version |
| `templates` | list project templates |
| `new <targetDir>` | create a project from a template |
| `new-level <project> <Name>` | scaffold a level and register it |
| `doctor <project>` | toolchain, manifest, scenes, lock, IDE config |
| `info <project>` | manifest paths, scenes, tools |
| `maps <project>` | map ids from the DLL, or scene filenames |
| `validate <project>` | manifest, scene ids, texture refs, `RW_GAME` |
| `build <project>` | configure + build GameLogic |
| `run <project>` | headless fixed-frame run |
| `lsp <project>` | write editor configs + compile database |
| `scene <sub> <project>` | list/add/set/remove/duplicate scene objects |
| `assets <sub> <project>` | list/import assets |

### templates

```text
rwcli templates --json
```

Lists the shipped template folders. Pass one to `new --template`.

### new

```text
rwcli new MyGame
rwcli new MyGame --template Empty2D --json
```

Creates a project, generates the IDE/tooling files, and prints next steps.
The target folder must not exist.

### new-level

```text
rwcli new-level . MyLevel
rwcli new-level . MyLevel --id LevelTwo --dry-run --json
```

Creates `<sourceDir>/MyLevel.h` and inserts `AddLevel<MyLevel>("MyLevel")`
before `Start(...)`. Idempotent; `--dry-run` prints the planned edits.

### doctor

```text
rwcli doctor . --json
rwcli doctor . --fix --json
```

`--fix` clears a stale `.raywaves/agent.lock`. Checks use `ok|warn|error`.

### info

```text
rwcli info . --json
```

Returns `project.{name,root,sourceDir,assetDir,entryDll,dllExists,sceneWidth,sceneHeight,targetFPS}`,
`scenes[]`, and `tools.{cmake,ninja,zig,raylib}`.

### build

```text
rwcli build . --json
rwcli build . --clean --jobs 8 --json
```

- Uses `.raywaves/build-agent`.
- Takes `.raywaves/agent.lock`; exits `7` if another live build owns it.
- `diagnostics[]` entries: `file`, `line`, `column`, `severity`, `message`.
- `rawTail` has the last build lines.

### run

```text
rwcli run . --frames 120 --json
rwcli run . --frames 120 --screenshot shot.png --state state.json --json
rwcli run . --frames 120 --input input.txt --json
```

Flags:

- `--frames N` default 60
- `--dt seconds` default `1/60`
- `--seed N` default 1
- `--screenshot path` project-relative or absolute
- `--screenshot-frame N` default last frame
- `--state path` writes the same state object to a file
- `--size WxH`
- `--timeout seconds` default 60
- `--visible` show the window
- `--audio` enable audio
- `--input script.txt` replay keys

Result:

```json
{"ok":true,"map":"Platformer2D","frames":120,"dt":0.0166667,
 "durationMs":900,"seed":1,"input":null,
 "screenshot":{"path":"...","bytes":38000,"nonEmpty":true},
 "entities":[{"id":1,"name":"Player","type":"Player",
              "position":[400,305],"size":[64,64],"rotation":0,"visible":true}],
 "state":{"rw.entity.count":1}}
```

Input script:

```text
# frame,key,down|up
0,KEY_RIGHT,down
30,KEY_RIGHT,up
0,mouse,640,360
```

`run` needs an OpenGL context even with the hidden window. Headless Linux hosts
need an X server: `xvfb-run -a` and, when there is no GPU driver,
`LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1`.

### lsp

```text
rwcli lsp . --json
rwcli lsp . --check --json
rwcli lsp . --force --json
```

- Writes `.clangd`, `.vscode/`, `AGENTS.md`, `.agents/skills/raywaves-game/`.
- Refreshes `.raywaves/tooling.ini` and both wrappers
  (`.raywaves/bin/rwcli.cmd` and `.raywaves/bin/rwcli`).
- Configures `.raywaves/build-ide` and copies `compile_commands.json` to the
  project root.
- `--check` runs `clangd --check` on `GameLogic/**/*.cpp` and returns
  `diagnostics[]`.
- `--force` overwrites generated configs.

### scene

```text
rwcli scene list . --json
rwcli scene list . --map Platformer2D --json
rwcli scene add . --map Platformer2D --name Crate --type decor --texture crate.png --position 620,300
rwcli scene add . --map Platformer2D --name Spawn --type spawn --position 620,300
rwcli scene set . --map Platformer2D --id 1 --position 700,300 --rotation 15 --visible 0
rwcli scene duplicate . --map Platformer2D --id 1
rwcli scene remove . --map Platformer2D --id 1
```

- `--map` is required when more than one `.scene` exists.
- `--type TAG` marks gameplay data (`spawn`, `enemy`, `decor`, ...).
- `--scale 2` or `--scale 2,3`
- `--layer N`
- `--dry-run` validates without writing.

### assets

```text
rwcli assets list . --json
rwcli assets import . /home/me/art/player.png
rwcli assets import . /home/me/art/player.png --force
```

Imported files land in `Assets/` with unsafe characters replaced by `_`.

## Exit codes

| Code | Meaning |
|---|---|
| 0 | success |
| 2 | usage error |
| 3 | project/validation/LSP error |
| 4 | build failed |
| 5 | run failed |
| 6 | timeout |
| 7 | locked by another process |
| 8 | game process crashed |

JSON failure shape:

```json
{"ok":false,"error":{"code":"build_failed","message":"..."},
 "diagnostics":[{"file":"GameLogic/Player.cpp","line":42,"column":7,
                 "severity":"error","message":"..."}],
 "rawTail":"..."}
```

## Common failures

- `rwcli` not recognized: use the generated project wrapper or the absolute path.
- `invalid_project`: pass the folder containing `project.raywaves`.
- `dll_missing`: run `build` first.
- `build_locked`: wait, or `doctor --fix` after the owner died.
- `clangd_missing`: install LLVM, then rerun `lsp --check`.
- Red stderr text with exit 0: normal logs; redirect `2>$null` (PowerShell) or
  `2>/dev/null` (bash).
- `run_window` on a headless host: run on a desktop session or under `xvfb-run -a`.
- Stale configs after moving the project or engine: `rwcli lsp . --force`.
